# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in ONE key. `.env` is git-ignored and is
# read only by server/classify.mjs — it never reaches the browser.
#
# Put it in the project root (next to package.json) OR in server/ — both are
# checked. On Windows make sure the name is exactly ".env" and not ".env.txt":
# in Explorer, View > File name extensions.
#
# Not working? Run:  npm run check
# It says where the file was found and whether the key is accepted.

# --- Groq (free tier) --------------------------------------------------------
# Get one at https://console.groq.com/keys
GROQ_API_KEY=gsk_...

# Model. Default is openai/gpt-oss-120b (production tier, supports tool calls).
# Other tool-capable options: llama-3.3-70b-versatile, llama-3.1-8b-instant,
# qwen/qwen3.6-27b. The server checks your key's model list at startup and
# tells you if the one you picked is not available.
# SANAD_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# --- or Anthropic ------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# SANAD_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5

# --- optional ----------------------------------------------------------------
# SANAD_PROVIDER=groq     # groq | anthropic | mock (mock = offline matcher, no key)
# SANAD_PORT=8787

# --- voice (optional) --------------------------------------------------------
# `npm run tts` pre-renders every spoken line to public/audio/, so read-aloud
# sounds like a person and works offline. Without it the app uses the browser's
# built-in voice — everything still works, it just sounds robotic.
#
# SANAD needs 124 Arabic clips (~9,500 characters). Set ONE of these; whichever
# key is present decides the provider. Test it with "npm run check".
#
# 1) Azure — RECOMMENDED. 500k characters/month free, forever, no credit card,
#    and the only option here with real IRAQI voices rather than MSA.
#    portal.azure.com > create a "Speech service" (F0 free tier) > Keys and Endpoint
# AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=eastus        # must match your resource's region
# TTS_VOICE_AR=ar-IQ-RanaNeural     # female; ar-IQ-BassemNeural is male
#
# 2) ElevenLabs — best quality. ~10k characters/month free, but the free tier
#    forbids commercial use: fine for a demo, not for release.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# TTS_VOICE_AR=                     # an ElevenLabs voice ID, not a name
#
# 3) Google Cloud — large free monthly quota, but billing must be enabled.
#    Arabic is ar-XA (Modern Standard), not Iraqi.
# GOOGLE_TTS_API_KEY=
# TTS_VOICE_AR=ar-XA-Wavenet-A
#
# 4) Groq — reuses the key above, but the free tier allows 100 clips per DAY,
#    so a full set takes two runs on two days. Speech models also need a
#    one-time terms click; the script prints the link when that happens.
# TTS_MODEL_AR=canopylabs/orpheus-arabic-saudi
# TTS_VOICE_AR=noura                # or fahad, sultan, lulwa, aisha, abdullah
#
# TTS_PROVIDER=azure    # force one when several keys are present
# TTS_LANGS=ar          # or ar,en to generate both
